            <ArticleTitle>Giant benign esophageal schwannoma requiring esophagectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>340-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Benign esophageal schwannomas are rare tumors with only 14 cases reported in the English literature. All previous reports describe excision without major esophageal resection. We report the case of a 33-year-old woman with a giant esophageal schwannoma that required total thoracic esophagectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
